oss (1.1.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Read a module blacklist from the files modprobe actually reads, instead of
    treating "the module is not loaded" as "the module is blacklisted". A stock
    kernel boots on about 130 of its ~6,900 modules, so on a fresh install 159
    of the 170 flags in the modprobe section reported as already applied when
    nothing was blacklisting them — and a flag that reads as in effect cannot be
    switched on, so those modules could not be selected either.
  * Say which file blacklists a module when it was not this app that wrote it,
    so a distro's own blacklist.conf is no longer reported as the user's choice.
  * Read /run, /lib and /usr/lib/modprobe.d as well as /etc/modprobe.d — the
    kernel package ships a blacklist of its own in /lib.
  * Treat hyphens and underscores in a module name as the same module, which is
    how modprobe treats them; half of a distro blacklist is written with hyphens.
  * Notice a blacklist added or removed in /etc/modprobe.d by hand, which
    previously left the section unchanged on screen.

 -- Jegly <jjjegly@gmail.com>  Mon, 17 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000

oss (1.0.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Merge the grub section into /etc/default/grub instead of writing a
    /etc/default/grub.d drop-in, and remove a stale drop-in from earlier
    releases on the next apply.
  * Stamp the banner on in-place login.defs edits, so the app can recognise
    its own writes instead of reporting every login.defs flag as "didn't take".
  * Preserve the existing mode on in-place writes, so applying grub settings
    no longer resets /etc/default/grub from 0600 back to 0644.
  * Drop net.ipv4/ipv6.conf.all.mc_forwarding: the sysfs entry is read-only,
    so those two flags could never apply and were in every shipped preset.
  * Show why a card is greyed out inside the card; a tooltip on an insensitive
    widget is never displayed.
  * Page through the unit and package browsers instead of capping them.
  * Read live mount state in the fstab section, and show drift from fstab.
  * Add the conf.default counterparts of the conf.all network settings, newer
    CPU mitigations (ITS, TSA, VMSCAPE), more SSH, auditd and desktop flags,
    and more firewall ports, postures and rule fields.

 -- Jegly <jjjegly@gmail.com>  Sun, 16 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000

oss (0.1.1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Back up and restore the configuration files themselves, to and from a
    portable archive, choosing which locations to include on both sides.
  * Fix the apply dialog freezing after a successful apply.
  * Report progress during Apply instead of a bare spinner.
  * Stop reading gsettings as root, where there is no session bus.
  * Read the firewall rule list on machines with application-profile rules,
    which previously failed to parse and took the whole section with them.
  * Remove packages successfully: the removal command carried --no-remove,
    which aborts on any removal at all.
  * Roll back on an unexpected error rather than leaving files written, and
    refuse a permissions change naming an account this machine lacks.
  * Survive `sysctl --system` failing on keys from files this app did not
    write, instead of blaming the transaction for the machine's own config.
  * Show a flag's switch as on when the setting is in effect, however it got
    that way, rather than only when this app staged it.
  * Keep the Apply-failed report inside a window that fits on the screen.
  * Open each section at its top, and make the section navigation strip work.

 -- Jegly <jjjegly@gmail.com>  Tue, 28 Jul 2026 12:45:00 +0000

